works.original:
Manopubbaṅgamā dhammā,
manoseṭṭhā manomayā;
Manasā ce paduṭṭhena,
bhāsati vā karoti vā;
Tato naṁ dukkhamanveti,
cakkaṁva vahato padaṁ.

works.translation:
In the name of the Lord of soul and wisdom,
beyond whom thought does not pass;
Lord of name and Lord of place,
Lord who gives daily bread, the guide;
Lord of Saturn and the turning sky,
who lights the Moon, Venus and the Sun.
